when I was 14\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "When fall came, she left for the Underworld.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The earth grew colder and darker then.<br/> <br/>", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Comparatives", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the comparative to compare two things.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The comparative ends in -er: <span class=\"italic\">taller </span> <br>Or, <span class=\"italic\">more</span>  is used with longer words: <span class=\"italic\">more beautiful</span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use the comparative with a noun:  <span class=\"italic\">a bigger car, his car was older.</span> <br> You can use the comparative with than: <span class=\"italic\">his house is larger than my house, this dress is more expensive than that one.</span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Persephone was more beautiful than other women.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The gods were not better.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The Underworld was a darker, more frightening place.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to believe", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to think that something is true or correct", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The Greeks believed in gods and goddesses.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le05ob01aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about myths.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "myth", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a traditional story explaining cultural beliefs", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The myth of Hercules is my favorite.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le05ob01aud02", "type": "audi